From 1cd17b731f62ef5fcb799f9f91ba39c14bb1e6b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Glib Shpychka <23005347+gshpychka@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:54:02 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix(agents): accept answers from the requester's chat after a
 subagent finishes

When a subagent finishes, OpenClaw continues the requester's session in an
internal turn. A question that turn asks only accepts answers from a caller
with the internal turn's authority, so a reply from the chat that started the
subagent is refused.

sessions_spawn records the requesting chat turn's caller facts on the subagent
run. The completion handoff carries the caller that every finished run shares,
and a verified handoff checks answers against that caller. Replies from other
senders, unverified handoffs, and revoked settle batches are still refused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
